This licence covers the build and app code in this repository: build.sh,
check.sh, index.html (template and app logic), and tools/*.py. It does not
cover the engine/ submodule, which is a separate repository (vocab-engine)
with its own MIT licence, or the pack data described below.

## Pack data

The data under `pack/` (words, sentences, passages, and the generated
sentences in `tools/*.tsv`) is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This reflects upstream share-alike terms: glosses come from Wiktionary via
kaikki.org (CC BY-SA 3.0), and frequency data comes from
hermitdave/FrequencyWords (CC BY-SA 4.0), both of which require share-alike
redistribution of derived data.

Example sentences are from Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR) and remain attributed by
contributor in `pack/attribution.json`.

Build-time tools and models used to construct this pack (part-of-speech
taggers such as spaCy or Stanza language models, some of which carry
non-commercial or GPL licences) are used only while building the pack and
ship nothing into the built output. They do not affect the licence of the
shipped code or pack data. See the "Sources and licences" table in
README.md for the full list of sources used per data type.
